From e0896242d40b084a6c1029902ac3beefd5031046 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 08:58:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban: a write the stopped Board sync keeps local
 says so, not "the live run gets this note"

Incident (2026-11-13, laptop-1): the gateway gave up the Board sync role (SchemaAhead) at 23:53 PT.
kanban_comment on t_01a1d3e55460fe21, whose live run was on worker-7, still returned
`live_run: true` and "the card has a live worker run: it gets this note at its next model call".
Comments 10761 (23:54), 10772 (00:15) and 10776 (00:22) sat in the local kanban_sync_outbox (pending,
0 attempts) and never reached the Board or the run; a chat told David a relayed request was delivered.

Five whys
- Root (happened): a design gap in the write path. The tool's delivery report is built without reading
  this gateway's sync state (tools/kanban_tools.py set `delivery` whenever `kb.live_run_id` on the local
  row was not None; hermes_cli/kanban.py printed the same line), so it reported a local write as
  delivered to a remote run.
- Root (not caught): no test ran a write tool while the sync role was given up; and the agent-side
  instructions had no rule to check `comment_delivered` on the Board before telling David a note was
  delivered (now in kanban-orchestrator references/stuck-card-recovery.md, "A comment or unblock that
  never arrives").
- Recurrence: three instances that night: 10761 at 23:54 from another chat (it noticed, nobody filed a
  fix), then 10772 at 00:15 and 10776 at 00:22 from chat 20261026_235722_bef6c6.
- Countermeasures: symptom: 10776's content was re-posted from worker-7 on t_01a1d40c10f38195
  (comment_delivered 00:44:12 PT, run 531). Root: this commit. Instructions: the skill section above.

Fix
- hermes_cli/kanban_board_delivery.py: `queued_local(conn, task_id)`: on a board that syncs
  (board_mode != off) while kanban_sync_runstate records the loop down (role given up, refused start,
  crash, stop), returns `board_delivery: "queued_local"` and `board_sync: "queued locally: this
  gateway's Board sync has been stopped since <time> (<reason>); other hosts and remote runs won't see
  this until it recovers"`. When another gateway holds the card's live run (lease_holder != own
  gateway), adds `live_run_host` and a `route` (`hermes kanban comment <id> "..."` on that host).
- Tools: the kanban handler wrapper annotates successful results of complete, block, unblock,
  schedule, continue, request_review, request_changes, comment, attach, attach_url, link, unlink and
  archive. A comment on a remote run gets that text as `delivery` instead of the live-run promise; a
  comment on a run on this host keeps the promise (the run reads this file). Healthy sync: unchanged
  (one config read + one stat, no board connection).
- CLI: `comment` drops the live-run line for a remote run and prints the notice; `link`, and every
  `_bulk_apply` caller passing conn (complete, block, schedule, unblock), print it once when anything
  was written.
- kanban_create is unchanged: its runs_on/placement paths already read runstate.

Proof
- tests/tools/test_kanban_board_delivery.py (12): the stopped state is made by the real run_forever
  (start check passes, first round meets SchemaAhead, records "gave up the sync role"); the remote run
  is a Board lease mirror applied with apply_remote_changes. RED on 43c2e75af2 (source reverted, tests
  kept): 6 failed (tool comment/unblock/link, local-run comment, CLI comment, CLI link); the healthy,
  unsynced and remote_runner cases passed. GREEN: 12 passed.
- Mutants (sdlc-review mutants.py, 11): 10 killed; survivor M3 (drop the early runstate.down() fast
  path) is equivalent: _stopped re-reads it; the fast path only avoids a board connection.
- 90 related files (tests/tools/test_kanban*.py, every test referencing kanban_comment / _bulk_apply /
  _cmd_comment|link|unblock, sync schema guard, pool-deny): 1730 passed, 3 skipped.
  scripts/check --base origin/main: 19 checks ok.
